From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:22:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 022/207] deepseek: prefer executable EXL3 siblings in CUDA
 rank plans

Restore Jay Leaton's published recipe 60b6688 CUDA storage-selection behavior through the current shared trellis validator. CUDA rank plans select EXL3 siblings while the shared projection API keeps dense-first ownership and existing format refusals.

Retain a header-only compressor regression on both ranks, including reversed shard order, dense-only refusal and malformed trellis refusal. Extend real-header inspection to full checkpoint coverage and make environment-driven header checks execute rather than reuse a skipped test result.
